@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ quiz_exclusions: [女王]
 
 ## Meaning
 
-太后 is an empress dowager or queen mother. JMdict glosses it as “empress dowager; queen mother,” and Digital Daijisen defines it as a title for a grand empress dowager (太皇太后) or an empress dowager (皇太后). In plain terms, Digital Daijisen describes 皇太后 as the empress of the previous emperor, or one who is also the current emperor's birth mother, and 太皇太后 as the empress of the emperor two reigns back.
+太后 is an empress dowager or queen mother. JMdict glosses it as “empress dowager; queen mother,” and Digital Daijisen defines it as a title for a grand empress dowager (太皇太后) or an empress dowager (皇太后). In plain terms, Digital Daijisen describes 太皇太后 as the empress of the emperor two reigns back and 皇太后 as the empress of the previous emperor; in a narrower sense, 皇太后 is such an empress who is also the current emperor's birth mother.
 
 - 太后は若い皇帝を支えました。 (たいこうはわかいこうていをささえました。) — The empress dowager supported the young emperor.
 - 歴史ドラマで、太后が大きな力を持つ場面がありました。 (れきしドラマで、たいこうがおおきなちからをもつばめんがありました。) — In a historical drama, there was a scene in which the empress dowager held great power.
